module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.KoszulConormalComparison

/-!
# Top cohomology of a normalized conormal comparison

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ, lemma-regular-immersion-ext, top cohomology calculation.
(blueprint: lem-sc-koszul-conormal-top-homology).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace ExteriorAlgebra

/-- A normalized comparison induces an isomorphism on top cohomology whenever the
specified conormal vectors form a basis. No vanishing in other degrees is assumed.
Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ, lemma-regular-immersion-ext, last paragraph of proof.
(blueprint: lem-sc-koszul-conormal-top-homology).

Proof: The standard top wedge e_top generates the rank-one module exterior^r E.
Evaluation at e_top identifies its dual with A. The next term is zero, so every
functional in degree r is a cocycle. For r>0, precomposition with contraction
of e_top has image the ideal generated by f: the complementary coordinate
functionals give each generator up to a unit sign, and every value is a linear
combination of those generators. Hence the top cohomology is A/I. For r=0
there is no incoming differential, the generating ideal is zero, and the same
identification holds. The given conormal basis b identifies the target normal
determinant with A/I by the ordered wedge of its dual basis. The determinant
pairing evaluates this generator on the ordered wedge of b to 1, and this
evaluation is a linear isomorphism for a finite free module of rank r.
Apply normalization to the standard basis vectors v i = Finsupp.single i 1.
Under these two identifications the induced top cohomology map is multiplication
by (-1)^(r*(r-1)/2), an invertible scalar. The homology of the single target in
degree r is its defining module, so the induced homology map is an isomorphism.
If I=A the quotient and both cohomology modules are zero. For r=0 the scalar is 1.
Neither this calculation nor its edge cases requires Koszul-regularity. -/
theorem koszul_conormal_comparison_isIso_top_homology
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → A)
    (hf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I)
    (b : Module.Basis (Fin r) (A ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)
    (hb : ∀ i, b i = koszulConormalVector A I r f hf (Finsupp.single i 1))
    (φ : koszulDualComplex A r f ⟶
      (HomologicalComplex.single (ModuleCat A) (ComplexShape.up ℕ) r).obj
        (koszulNormalDeterminant A I r))
    (hφ : IsKoszulConormalComparison A I r f hf φ) :
    IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap φ r) := by sorry

end ExteriorAlgebra
